#!/usr/bin/env python3
# -*- coding: utf-8 -*-
"""acczLOL — one-file Telegram bot, Mini App, admin UI and MTProto worker.

INSTALL (Python 3.11+):
    python -m pip install 'aiohttp>=3.10,<4' 'cryptography>=43' 'Telethon>=1.45,<2' 'qrcode[pil]>=8,<9' 'psycopg[binary]>=3.2,<4'
CONFIGURE:
    python bot.py --setup
RUN:
    python bot.py
DEMO (no Telegram credentials, no real payments):
    python bot.py --demo --port 8080
TESTS:
    python bot.py --self-test

RENDER / NEON:
    Build: pip install "aiohttp>=3.10,<4" "cryptography>=43" "Telethon>=1.45,<2" "qrcode[pil]>=8,<9" "psycopg[binary]>=3.2,<4"
    Start: python bot.py --host 0.0.0.0 --port $PORT
    DATABASE_URL: your private Neon PostgreSQL connection string (optional).
    ENCRYPTION_KEY: permanent Fernet key, required with DATABASE_URL.
    Generate once: python -c "from cryptography.fernet import Fernet; print(Fernet.generate_key().decode())"
    LTC_ADDRESS: your mainnet Litecoin receiving address (optional override).
    ADMIN_IDS: comma-separated moderator Telegram IDs for payment notifications.
    The database tables are created/migrated automatically; no SQL setup is needed.
    Payment assets: LTC, BNB, USDT/USDC on BSC, TRX, USDT on TRON and NEAR.
    Existing local SQLite data is not automatically copied into a new Neon database.

MARKETPLACE:
    Any signed-in user can connect an owned account by phone, Telegram code and 2FA.
    Optional mail.tm login email is created and verified through official Telegram methods.
    Telegram can reject a domain or forbid email changes; this is reported, never bypassed.
    Login email and 2FA recovery email are different; the latter is not changed.
    Sale proceeds are credited once, only after successful fulfillment.
    Withdrawals: >=100 RUB in any supported asset and network; funds reserved on request, refunded on rejection.
    Moderator confirms actual deposits and payouts in the bot or admin web interface.
    Deposits require no transaction hash; a pending button never credits money by itself.
    Mini App checks owner-scoped events every 2 seconds and shows the pixel bot success animation.
    All credentials and pending phone flows are encrypted. No secrets are written to logs.

Required: BOT_TOKEN, PUBLIC_URL (your HTTPS origin), TELEGRAM_API_ID,
TELEGRAM_API_HASH from my.telegram.org. A real authorized StringSession or
Telethon .session is uploaded by the administrator; no account login is faked.
Site pictures, fonts, HTML, CSS and JS are embedded below. Premium Telegram
emoji are resolved through Bot API after the bot is connected.
The program creates acczlol_data/store.sqlite3 and a private encryption key.
Use a persistent disk for SQLite DATA_DIR, or configure DATABASE_URL + ENCRYPTION_KEY for Neon. Keep its encryption key when migrating.
ADMIN_KEY can override the supplied administrator key. Its default is stored
only as a salted PBKDF2 digest, never in HTML, JS or the database as plaintext.
ADMIN_IDS may limit administrator access to comma-separated Telegram IDs.

Optional processes, using the SAME DATA_DIR/key: --role web, --role bot,
--role agent. Default --role all runs the components as isolated async tasks.
SQLite WAL is suitable for a single-host shop. PostgreSQL uses transaction advisory locks for balance operations.

Mini App authentication: validated Telegram initData -> opaque server session.
Standalone browser authentication: /login command in the bot -> one-use app code.
Deposits: Decimal crypto/RUB quote, the address for the chosen network, manual admin
approval without a required transaction hash, atomic ledger credit. Clicking 'paid' never
credits money by itself. No smart contract or automatic blockchain settlement
is implied. Quote uses CoinGecko, with Kraken LTC/USD × CBR USD/RUB fallback.
Quotes round up at the precision used by each payment method.

Purchases: atomic balance debit + stock reservation; the worker validates the
authorized account session, completes delivery or refunds the hold atomically.
Only a paid order's buyer can request a fresh Telegram login code. The worker
reads service dialog 777000, not other chats. It does NOT initiate a new login
on behalf of a stranger. Buyer requests login in Telegram, then presses Get code.
2FA passwords are provided with stock and encrypted; unknown existing cloud
passwords cannot be recovered from Telegram. .tdata is not a .session file.

Premium emoji/button IDs are the supplied IDs. Telegram may require Premium
on the bot owner or Fragment eligibility. Unsupported icons fall back to emoji.
Fullscreen uses expand() and requestFullscreen() on supported Telegram 8.0+
clients, safe-area events and a manual retry button when the client refuses.

No bot token, MTProto key, payment approval or real account is supplied by this
file. The runnable integration requires your actual credentials and sessions.
"""
